---
import PillBadge from '../ui/PillBadge.astro';
import PullQuote from '../ui/PullQuote.astro';
import ScrollReveal from '../ui/ScrollReveal.astro';

/**
 * "Why now — Plan A or Plan B"
 * Sets up the dual-tier offer narratively (The Hedge / The Move) before
 * the pricing reveal. Carries the historical pull quote that used to
 * anchor the History section.
 */
---

<section class="section-y bg-bone" id="why-now">
  <div class="container-edge">
    <ScrollReveal class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <div class="flex flex-col items-center gap-5 text-center">
        <PillBadge>Why now</PillBadge>
        <h2
          class="font-display text-ink text-balance"
          style="font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 4.4vw, 3.6rem); line-height: 1.06; font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 96, 'wght' 380;"
        >
          Plan A. Or Plan B.
        </h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted text-pretty md:text-xl">
          Founders come to us for one of two reasons.
        </p>
      </div>
    </ScrollReveal>

    <div class="mx-auto mt-14 grid max-w-5xl grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-8">
      <!-- Plan B -->
      <ScrollReveal>
        <article class="flex h-full flex-col gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-border-soft bg-bone-deeper/40 p-8 md:p-10">
          <h3
            class="flex items-baseline gap-3 font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl"
            style="font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 96, 'wght' 420;"
          >
            <span class="text-brass">Plan B.</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-[1rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-muted text-pretty md:text-[1.05rem]">
            You're not sure what the next five years look like at home. You're not predicting anything in particular &mdash; you just want a real option, fully prepared, ready to activate. Not a passport you bought and forgot in a drawer. A working second base, with residency filed, your CPA briefed, your apartment in a country you've already visited.
          </p>
        </article>
      </ScrollReveal>

      <!-- Plan A -->
      <ScrollReveal>
        <article class="flex h-full flex-col gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-oxblood/15 bg-oxblood/5 p-8 md:p-10">
          <h3
            class="flex items-baseline gap-3 font-display text-2xl text-ink md:text-3xl"
            style="font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 96, 'wght' 420;"
          >
            <span class="text-oxblood">Plan A.</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-[1rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-muted text-pretty md:text-[1.05rem]">
            You're tired of the noise. You want a quieter main base &mdash; somewhere the news doesn't dominate the dinner table, where your kids can grow up trilingual without trying, where Sunday is genuinely a slower day. You're not running from anything. You're choosing where you build the next decade.
          </p>
        </article>
      </ScrollReveal>
    </div>

    <ScrollReveal class="mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl text-center">
      <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-muted md:text-[1.05rem]">
        Both reasons are valid. Neither requires a strong political opinion. The point is having the option, structured cleanly, before you need it.
      </p>
    </ScrollReveal>

    <ScrollReveal class="mt-14 flex justify-center">
      <PullQuote>
        The cost of moving early is paperwork. The cost of moving late is everything.
      </PullQuote>
    </ScrollReveal>
  </div>
</section>
